            <ArticleTitle>Down Syndrome Screening in India: Are We There Yet?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>393-399</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s13224-017-1042-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Down syndrome is the most common cause of intellectual disability among live born children and is amenable to prenatal detection. Screening for Down syndrome on a population basis requires a thorough understanding of the principles involved in the screening tests. We discuss the rationale behind the commonly available screening tests and the Indian scenario in this setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
